[style name="Interaction_Style"]
if {Dead_person_choice} != 0:
	if {Dead_person_choice} == 1:
		join Town_Leader rightmost
		join Thorinn (normal) leftmost
		Town_Leader: Thorinn, you've saved them! [b]Truly[/b], you are a gift to Rockfall!
		Thorinn: Lets not [b]forget[/b] the one who paid the ultimate price.
		Town_Leader: The lives of others in not to be played with. I do understand however that dire circumstances call for desperate measures.
		Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
		Malrik: What will you do now [i]doctor...?
		- Publicly credit Malric
			set {Blame_choice} = 2
			Thorinn: This cure wasn't mine alone. Malric's knowledge made this possible.
			Town_Leader: [b]Malric?[/b] That explains... I'd hoped never to hear that name again.
			Town_Leader: But if what you say is the truth, then even in the darkest of souls you can find a spark of light.
			Town_Leader: Do be [i]careful[/i], even thogh he was of great help this time, following his ways will lead to a dangerous path we do not condone.
			update Town_Leader (invis)
			Thorinn: *Turning to Malric in the shadows*
			join Malrik rightmost
			Malrik: A [i]rare[/i] day, doctor. They don't hate me quite as much... for now. You have my thanks.
		- Accept the credit
			set {Blame_choice} = 1
			Thorinn (normal): I just did what had to be done.
			Thorinn: Vivian was the purest soul that managed to save e[i]veryone.[/i] Lets honour her by never forgetting her kindness.
		- Thank Malric in private
			set {Blame_choice} = 3
			Thorinn: I just did what had to be done.
			update Town_Leader (invis)
			join Malrik rightmost
			Thorinn: *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
			Thorinn: I [b]know[/b] I didn't mention you, but know this, you have my thanks.
			Thorinn: Without your help I wouldn't have been [i]able[/i] to create the antidote.
			Malrik: So that's how it is. I had hoped for a glimpse of salvation in return. Secrets weigh [b]heavy[/b] doctor.
	
	elif {Dead_person_choice} == 2:
		join Town_Leader rightmost
		join Thorinn (agitated) leftmost
		Town_Leader: Thorinn, you tried your best, but this time it was [b]not[/b] enough.
		Town_Leader: Only one saved and so many lost. Couldn't you have done [i]more?
		Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
		Malrik: What will you do now doctor...?
		- Admit fault
			set {Blame_choice} = 1
			Thorinn (agitated): I really did the best I could.
			Town_Leader: Your capabilities as a doctor have proven to be [b]less[/b] than what you've promised.
		- Publicly blame Malric
			set {Blame_choice} = 2
			Thorinn: This failure [b]wasn't[/b] mine alone. Malric's evil ways made this possible.
			Town_Leader: [b]Malric?[/b] That explains... I'd hoped never to hear that name again.
			Thorinn: He led me astray with his [b]twisted words!
			update Town_Leader (invis)
			join Malrik rightmost
			Malrik: ...!
			Malrik: [b]You've got no idea whose name you've just tarnished.
		- Confront Malric in private
			set {Blame_choice} = 3
			Thorinn (agitated): I really did the best I could.
			Town_Leader: Your capabilities as a doctor have proven to be [b]less[/b] than what you've [i]promised.
			update Town_Leader (invis)
			Thorinn (agitated): *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
			join Malrik rightmost
			Thorinn: I [b]didn't[/b] expose you, but know this, you also had a hand in this failure and I'll never forgive you for it.
			Malrik: I've warned you [i]sufficiently[/i] [b]but[/b] you did not want to listen because your judgement was clouded by the rumours fed to you by the [b]village.
	
	elif {Dead_person_choice} == 3:
		join Town_Leader rightmost
		join Thorinn (agitated) leftmost
		Town_Leader: Thorinn, you tried your best but you only [i]half[/i] succeeded.
		Town_Leader: You [b]killed[/b] one of us to save three, and yet, two more are dead. Was it worth the life of an innocent?
		Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
		Malrik: What will you do now doctor...?
		- Accept the responsibility
			set {Blame_choice} = 1
			Thorinn: I did what was in my power.
			Town_Leader: We might [i]disagree[/i] if this was the right choice, but Astrid's sacrifice saved three lives.
			Town_Leader: Let's forever honour her memory.
		- Publicly put the responsibility on Malric
			set {Blame_choice} = 2
			Thorinn: This cure [b]wasn't[/b] mine alone. Malric's knowledge made this possible.
			Town_Leader: [b]Malric?[/b] That explains... I'd hoped never to hear that name again.
			Thorinn: I'm not guilt free, but if Malric didn't [b]trick me[/b], this could've been avoided.
			Thorinn: I will make sure not to trust Malric's misleading words from now on.
			update Town_Leader (invis)
			join Malrik rightmost
			Malrik: ...!
			Malrik: [b]You've got no idea whose name you've just tarnished.
		- Confront Malric in private
			set {Blame_choice} = 3
			Thorinn: I did what was in my power.
			update Town_Leader (invis)
			Thorinn: *Turning to Malric in the shadows* So...listen.
			join Malrik rightmost
			Thorinn: I didn't mention you, but know this, [i]you had a hand in this aswell.
			Thorinn: Your cryptic messages caused this loss.
			Malrik: I've warned you [i]sufficiently.
			Malrik: It isn't my fault that you didn't trust my word enough, as your judgement was clouded by the rumours fed to you by the village.
	
	elif {Dead_person_choice} == 4:
		join Town_Leader rightmost
		join Thorinn (agitated) leftmost
		Town_Leader: Thorinn, you came with hope and promises, but we are left with grief. Five lives were lost under your care. You had a strong opinion, doctor, but you should've consulted us.
		Malrik: *Malric whispers from the shadows* Psst.
		Malrik: Seems like your good intentions [b]weren't[/b] of much help this time. What will you tell them now?
		- Admit fault
			set {Blame_choice} = 1
			Thorinn (agitated): I tried to find a way that wouldn’t cause [b]more harm[/b] than what was already done, but in the end, I failed them. I will always carry this burden.
			Town_Leader: You speak of [i]burdens[/i], but what about the mourning families? You had a [b]choice[/b], doctor, and you chose [b]wrong.
		
		- Publicly blame Malric
			set {Blame_choice} = 2
			Thorinn (agitated): I admit that I did [i]know[/i] of a cure, but it was based on [b]Malric's twisted words.
			Thorinn: I had a choice to make, a [i][b]terrible[/b][/i] choice, take an innocent life or let these people die. I just couldn't cross that line.
			Thorinn: Malric is too far gone in his ways of dark magic, there [i]wasn't even[/i] a guarantee this was going to work.
			Town_Leader: I understand you didn't want to give into Malric's dishonourable ways.
			update Town_Leader (invis)
			join Malrik rightmost
			Malrik: ...!
			Malrik: [b]You've got no idea whose name you've just tarnished.
	else:
	[signal arg="start_night"]
	update Thorinn (invis)
	update Town_Leader (invis)
	update Malrik (invis)
	[wait time="2.0"]
	[signal arg="Start_summary"]
elif {Ian.Selected_Ian_Choice} == 0:
	if {Favian.Talked_to} == false:
		set {Favian.Talked_to} = true
		join Thorinn leftmost
		join Town_Leader rightmost
		Town_Leader: [i]Who are you[/i], outsider? And what business do you have here?
		Thorinn: I'm Thorinn, a [b]doctor from Stoneleaf.[/b] Hugo told me your pharmacist has fallen ill. I've come to see if I can help him.
		Town_Leader: *grumbles* [b]That Hugo...[/b] always dragging strangers into town with his inn.
		Thorinn: And who might you be?
		Town_Leader: The name's [i]Favian.[/i] I'm the current [b]town leader of Rockfall.[/b] My family's run this town for g[i]enerations.
		Town_Leader: It's true Ian's been sick for a while. His absence has taken a toll on the village.
		Town_Leader: More of my people are starting to feel ill, and without proper care, [i]they might not make it.
		Town_Leader: [b]Fine,[/b] do what you came here for and leave please. We already have a pharmasist, we don't need you here once he feels better.
	else:
		Town_Leader: Do what you must and [i]leave please.[/i] We already have a pharmacist, we don't need you here once he feels better.
